 "notes": "Prompt says 'IAM user policy attachment'; GT uses aws_iam_policy_attachment with users, so both attachment resource types are accepted. Resolved names with random suffix are unknown at plan, so name defaults are checked via variable defaults or declared name text. S3 key composition (s3_folder prefix) is not checked: GT builds it in a local. Read-only scope ('no write actions') cannot be expressed as a negative over a JSON policy string, so only the granted actions are checked. The 'execution directory' location of the source file is not checked (path.cwd vs relative path are equivalent). bucket_tagged requires the Name tag to carry the bucket name (zedcloud or a bucket-name reference), not merely any tag. upload_source requires the source path to reference image_filename, its stated default my-file.qcow2 (a bare var reference is shown resolved to that default in __declared__), or a local named for the image/file. Attachment's policy and user refs are tested as two refs and are not bound to one attachment resource (one attachment is the normal case)."
